                <pb facs="0076" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/18878: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-23T18:00:00+02:00">January 23, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 24—5:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. My 119, January 21, 7 p.m. As further facts regarding the circumstances
                    surrounding the altercation between the King and the Foreign Minister on the
                    Vichy severance question have come to light the British appear to be taking an
                    increasingly serious view of the influence being exerted by certain elements in
                    the King’s entourage. The present status of the matter is understood to be that
                    the British Embassy has recommended to London the taking of firm measures to
                    effect the removal from the Palace of certain undesirable persons particularly
                    the Assistant Chief of the Royal Cabinet who is reputed to be close to Aly Maher
                    Pasha and 16 or 17 Italians who are still connected with the Palace in various
                    capacities but that London has not yet indicated its reaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
